---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';

const lastUpdated = '20 May 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="Privacy notice for MadDogWarner.com.">
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="// privacy.notice" title="Privacy" text={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated} AEST`} />

      <div class="notice surface-card">
        <p>
          This page is a general privacy notice for MadDogWarner.com. It is written for transparency
          across common privacy frameworks, including Australian Privacy Principles, GDPR/UK GDPR-style
          transparency expectations, and California notice-at-collection concepts. It is not legal advice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content">
        <h2>Who operates this site</h2>
        <p>
          This site is operated under the online identity <strong>MadDogWarner</strong>. No real-name
          identity is published on the site.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
          The site is currently a static website. It does not provide user accounts, checkout, newsletter
          signup, comments, contact forms, advertising pixels, or application login.
        </p>
        <p>The following limited technical data may still be processed when you visit:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>standard web server and CDN logs, such as IP address, request URL, user agent, referrer, timestamp, and response status</li>
          <li>browser requests to third-party font infrastructure when Google Fonts are loaded</li>
          <li>information you voluntarily disclose if you contact MadDogWarner outside this website</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why data may be processed</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>to serve the website and requested pages</li>
          <li>to maintain availability, performance, and operational resilience</li>
          <li>to detect abuse, troubleshoot faults, and protect the site from malicious traffic</li>
          <li>to respond to voluntary communications received outside the website</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Legal basis and transparency</h2>
        <p>
          Where GDPR or UK GDPR concepts apply, the likely basis for limited technical processing is
          legitimate interests in operating, securing, and maintaining a static website. Where consent is
          legally required for a future feature, that feature should not be enabled until an appropriate
          consent or preference mechanism exists.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not currently set first-party analytics or marketing cookies. If analytics,
          embedded media, advertising, comments, or newsletter tooling are added later, this notice should
          be updated before those features go live.
        </p>

        <h2>Sharing and third parties</h2>
        <p>Data may be processed by service providers that are technically necessary to deliver the site, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>hosting, CDN, DNS, and security providers</li>
          <li>Google Fonts infrastructure for font delivery</li>
          <li>GitHub when you follow external repository links</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This site does not sell personal information and does not intentionally share personal information
          for cross-context behavioural advertising.
        </p>

        <h2>International processing</h2>
        <p>
          Because this is a public website delivered through global internet infrastructure, technical data
          may be processed in countries outside your location. Service provider processing is governed by
          the relevant provider terms and controls.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Static site content does not require visitor profiles. Technical logs, if retained by hosting or
          security providers, should be kept only as long as required for operations, diagnostics, security,
          abuse prevention, or legal compliance.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, object to,
          or receive a copy of personal information, and to complain to a privacy regulator. These rights may
          be limited where the site operator does not hold identifiable visitor records.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          The site is designed as a static deployment with no database, no authentication layer, and no
          intentional collection of sensitive personal information. Security headers are configured for
          baseline browser protection. Do not submit secrets, credentials, health information, or other
          sensitive data through any channel unless explicitly requested through a secure process.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          This notice should be reviewed whenever analytics, contact forms, newsletters, embedded content,
          comments, account features, or other data-collecting functionality is added.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-top: 5rem;
  }

  .notice {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .notice p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .content {
    max-width: 78ch;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.7rem;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>

